@NAME@ @VERSION@ -- a custom AI for Beyond All Reason
@DESCRIPTION@

Source, changelog and where to report problems: @URL@

WHO NEEDS THIS
  Only the player HOSTING the game. Everyone else just joins the lobby.

WINDOWS
  Close BAR. Right-click the zip, choose "Extract All...", open the extracted
  folder and double-click Install.bat. It finds BAR, copies the AI into BAR's
  data folder and switches the lobby to its full AI list (the simple list
  hides every custom AI).

LINUX
  tar xzf @SHORT@-@VERSION@-LINUX.tar.gz && sh install.sh
  It looks in ~/.local/share/BeyondAllReason and the usual Flatpak and Steam
  places. If BAR is elsewhere: sh install.sh "/path/to/BAR data folder"

INSTALL BY HAND
  1. Find BAR's data folder, the one holding engine, games and maps:
       Windows: <BAR install>\data   (usually
                C:\Users\<you>\AppData\Local\Programs\Beyond-All-Reason\data)
       Linux:   ~/.local/share/BeyondAllReason
  2. Copy the folder payload\@SHORT@ from this archive into <data>\AI\Skirmish\
     so that this file exists:
       <data>\AI\Skirmish\@SHORT@\@VERSION@\AIInfo.lua
     Remove any other version folder under @SHORT@: a hosted game loads the
     highest one by name, and "0.10.0" sorts below "0.9.0".
  3. With BAR closed, make an empty file named devmode.txt in <data>.
     Start BAR, open Settings > Developer and untick "Simple AI list".
  4. In a skirmish or a lobby you host, Add AI and pick @SHORT@ @VERSION@
     (the lobby lists AIs by their short name; the long name is "@NAME@").

NOTES
  - The AI lives in the data folder, not the engine folder, so a BAR engine
    update keeps it. Tested on BAR engine @ENGINE@.
  - Close BAR before installing: a loaded AI cannot be replaced.
  - Uninstall: delete <data>\AI\Skirmish\@SHORT@.
